<title>UK: MOTORCYCLING-FACTFILE ON WORLD CHAMPION DOOHAN.</title>
<headline>MOTORCYCLING-FACTFILE ON WORLD CHAMPION DOOHAN.</headline>
<dateline>DONINGTON PARK, England 1997-08-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a factfile on Australian Michael Doohan, who clinched his fourth consecutive 500cc world title on Sunday:</p>
<p>Born: Brisbane, Australia, June 4, 1965</p>
<p>Unmarried, lives with girlfriend Selina in Monaco</p>
<p>Racing career:</p>
<p>1974 - Had his first bike, a Honda MR50</p>
<p>1984 - First road race on a Yamaha</p>
<p>1987 - Raced Australian superbikes, Suzuka eight-hour</p>
<p>1989 - First 500cc Grand Prix, Japan. Scored his first</p>
<p>championship point that season and also his first podium finish</p>
<p>with a third place in the West German Grand Prix.</p>
<p>1990 - First pole position (Spain), first win (Hungary)</p>
<p>World championship progression:</p>
<p>1989 - 81 points, ninth overall</p>
<p>1990 - 179 points, 3rd (1 win)</p>
<p>1991 - 224 points, 2nd (3 wins)</p>
<p>1992 - 136 points, 2nd (5 wins) -- injured</p>
<p>1993 - 120 points, 8th (1 win)</p>
<p>1994 - 317 points, 1st (9 wins)</p>
<p>1995 - 248 points, 1st (7 wins)</p>
<p>1996 - 309 points, 1st (8 wins)</p>
<p>1997 (to date) - 270 points, (10 wins)</p>
<p>Total wins to date: 44</p>
<p>Total pole positions: 46</p>
<p>Total Grand Prix starts/finishes: 117/105</p>
<p>Total top three finishes: 80</p>
<p>Note - Has always raced for Honda in Grands Prix.</p>
</text>
